  The 'flat' row scores ONE fixed signature table against each test month. It
  still varies across horizons, because the months differ -- some months are
  simply harder than others. That is exactly why the gain row is the thing to
  read: it cancels the month-to-month difficulty and leaves only what letting
  the signatures move is worth.

  The mixture is the last training month's weights at every horizon, so the
  gain row isolates what letting the signatures move is worth -- and how fast
  that is used up.

